From: MedyMa <aneylovemzy@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6.6 v2] net: sfp: warm-reboot recovery via TX_DISABLE + I2C recovery

On warm reboot SFP modules stay powered while the kernel restarts,
potentially leaving the I2C state machine stuck.  Detect this by
checking mod-def0 at sfp_probe() time — if already asserted, the
module survived a warm reboot.

  - Pulse TX_DISABLE 300 ms + settle 500 ms, retry up to 3×.
  - Recover I2C bus via i2c_recover_bus().

Cold boot is unaffected: mod-def0 is not yet asserted when
sfp_probe() runs.

v2: 300 ms pulse, 500 ms settle, 3 retries, I2C recovery.

Signed-off-by: MedyMa <aneylovemzy@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/phy/sfp.c | 31 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c
@@ -3348,4 +3348,35 @@ static int sfp_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		}
 	}
 
+	/* Warm-boot recovery: module stayed powered → I2C/PHY may be stuck.
+	 * mod-def0 already asserted → pulse TX_DISABLE 300ms, wait 500ms,
+	 * retry 3×, then recover I2C bus.  Cold boot: mod-def0 not yet ready.
+	 */
+	if (sfp->gpio[0] && !IS_ERR(sfp->gpio[0]) &&
+	    gpiod_get_value_cansleep(sfp->gpio[0])) {
+		int retry;
+
+		if (sfp->gpio[3] && !IS_ERR(sfp->gpio[3])) {
+			for (retry = 0; retry < 3; retry++) {
+				dev_info(&pdev->dev,
+					 "warm boot: TX_DISABLE pulse %d/3\n",
+					 retry + 1);
+				gpiod_set_value_cansleep(sfp->gpio[3], 1);
+				msleep(300);
+				gpiod_set_value_cansleep(sfp->gpio[3], 0);
+				msleep(500);
+
+				if (gpiod_get_value_cansleep(sfp->gpio[0]))
+					break;
+			}
+		}
+
+		if (sfp->i2c)
+			i2c_recover_bus(sfp->i2c);
+
+		if (!gpiod_get_value_cansleep(sfp->gpio[0]))
+			dev_warn(&pdev->dev,
+				 "warm boot: module not responding after reset\n");
+	}
+
 	if (sfp->need_poll)
